      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Recreating a dropped unique index can fail if duplicate keys exist at completion, including duplicates written during the build; recovery may require data cleanup or write controls. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f9b9b0af7787e4449e51ccdb03429889b661d27a955462a3756bcd6c6445d67b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
