        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Hiding a candidate index before dropping it permits a query-performance trial and avoids rebuilding if the index is needed; Atlas documentation says unhiding takes less time than rebuilding a dropped index. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/performance-advisor/drop-indexes.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f6c4add550607d6262109b6caf6a81826bf3dc4a9cd84eae6cb4aaf0fcef99b5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:c446e63489aa8446b1d71f2772b7cf79421a58975649f29fc6246ce1f41f2967",
            "ev:f072ea71a34cd8083f75d3ce36c6f580da9e91cb35a998ceb2c831eb34fa46c8"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/new-in-mongodb-4-4-hidden-index/",
            "https://studio3t.com/knowledge-base/3t-build/desktop-ide/mongodb-index-strategy/",
            "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/DRIVERS-816"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A conventional index rebuild scans collection documents, generates and sorts index keys, and loads the resulting index. It uses memory and can spill temporary build data to disk; restoring an index definition alone does not restore the built index. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f645c8fdd5733f78e2cdf2cfa61db5393bbdadbc7b318da0403ba0d2067b8b21",
          "validationStatus": "NOT-SAMPLED",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/mongo/db/index_builds/README.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Building an index competes for CPU and I/O resources. On a write-heavy collection, an index build can reduce write performance and take longer, so recovery planning must account for production load. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:30add5fc7da2c9f53f40a39328a122568e4501045dcf6b04bd4cc3de5d8547f4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0ae5de966e86aff9b0014d68c35734da4aa9b2db78f947923bc0a73401046d92",
            "ev:67d80801faab394ec58fc61ac70f34b97edcf427035a9f57521159701563dc01"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/how-to-perform-rolling-index-builds-with-percona-operator-for-mongodb/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A hidden index still receives write updates and consumes storage and memory. Hiding is a trial of query-planner impact, not realization of the storage and maintenance savings expected from dropping the index. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/performance-advisor/drop-indexes.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3f8477346d5ab6449240e34c4850e074303cbd01104f5dc512307cf0ded124ca",
          "validationStatus": "NOT-SAMPLED",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://studio3t.com/knowledge-base/3t-build/desktop-ide/mongodb-index-strategy/",
            "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/DRIVERS-816",
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/new-in-mongodb-4-4-hidden-index/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hiding a unique index preserves its uniqueness constraint, and hiding a TTL index preserves document expiry. A hide trial therefore does not simulate removal of these index functions. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://studio3t.com/knowledge-base/3t-build/desktop-ide/mongodb-index-strategy/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3dfc5c27567ee4907ff5906a680bea5adcb154534ce3b9c90a0ed8f467cac733",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a8b52ab570009ca13c4d7a719b43c41966b54400b849805cbcdc768577bccb3a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/new-in-mongodb-4-4-hidden-index/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Optimized MongoDB index builds hold an exclusive collection lock at the beginning and end, while allowing interleaved reads and writes during the main build. Allowing concurrent traffic does not eliminate build resource consumption or performance impact. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4dc9774363384fbdfd72a663e67fc687ae021381ece3a11cd1511a51f27df075",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0ae5de966e86aff9b0014d68c35734da4aa9b2db78f947923bc0a73401046d92",
            "ev:6fa6c0722a1ea05599f1ec5efcce04c7977b160b7c3863e760e99f0fe0c1d401"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/how-to-perform-rolling-index-builds-with-percona-operator-for-mongodb/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For a showback decision, treat rebuild resource use and degraded application performance as possible offsets to recurring savings from a drop. This is a cost-accounting inference from the documented mechanisms, not a measured financial outcome or a fixed rebuild price. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/performance-advisor/drop-indexes.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d08dc973cbdbf0bd9845a209823175eecdc557d18f7d48c5a03eab8b0cf221b3",
          "validationStatus": "NOT-SAMPLED",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
            "https://www.percona.com/blog/how-to-perform-rolling-index-builds-with-percona-operator-for-mongodb/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Heavy writes during an index build can reduce write performance and lengthen the build; MongoDB recommends considering a window that reduces or stops writes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0c30288c546e37a5935fd2f812204ac7e0191de089b9962f557e74cd15ba0842",
          "validationStatus": "NOT-SAMPLED",
          "evidenceIds": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Replicated index builds run across data-bearing replica-set members and require a commit quorum. With the documented votingMembers quorum, an unreachable voting data-bearing member can stall completion. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/index-creation/",
